{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20118",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 4.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.59,
      "end_seconds": 14.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.9,
      "end_seconds": 25.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Doctor, it's pain going down the back of my left leg. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.04,
      "end_seconds": 30.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.91,
      "end_seconds": 38.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Two months, I think... sorry, about a month, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.27,
      "end_seconds": 49.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Right, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.88,
      "end_seconds": 57.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "It settles a little with walking and lying flat. It's worse with sitting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.77,
      "end_seconds": 65.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.16,
      "end_seconds": 77.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "It, It usually comes with tingling in my left foot. The tingling in my left foot? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.51,
      "end_seconds": 86.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any numbness between the legs or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.08,
      "end_seconds": 93.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "No numbness between the legs or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.65,
      "end_seconds": 100.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Have you had any weakness in the foot, bladder problems or bowel problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.29,
      "end_seconds": 105.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.95,
      "end_seconds": 108.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.85,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.48,
      "end_seconds": 120.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Alright, any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.47,
      "end_seconds": 125.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I mean, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.73,
      "end_seconds": 139.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.02,
      "end_seconds": 148.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "So, it's valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day. I take paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.07,
      "end_seconds": 151.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.95,
      "end_seconds": 158.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "1 gram, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.15,
      "end_seconds": 167.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.32,
      "end_seconds": 171.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.93,
      "end_seconds": 174.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.53,
      "end_seconds": 178.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.38,
      "end_seconds": 184.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.88,
      "end_seconds": 190.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.89,
      "end_seconds": 201.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Understood. Alright, high blood pressure, that matches what I have here. Alright, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.25,
      "end_seconds": 205.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.15,
      "end_seconds": 210.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.81,
      "end_seconds": 223.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.42,
      "end_seconds": 248.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 126 over 82, heart rate 64, temperature is 36.9 degrees, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.9,
      "end_seconds": 253.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.22,
      "end_seconds": 256.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.71,
      "end_seconds": 260.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.81,
      "end_seconds": 285.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Straight leg raising on the left brings on the leg pain at about forty degrees, and the power and reflexes are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.92,
      "end_seconds": 290.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.53,
      "end_seconds": 330.51,
      "duration_seconds": 27.98,
      "text": "I'm going to order blood tests, for back pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's get an MRI of the lower back, for sciatica. We'll begin with naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, for one week. You take it by mouth. That's for back and leg pain. Stay active and keep walking, bed rest makes this slower to settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.35,
      "end_seconds": 356.37,
      "duration_seconds": 24.02,
      "text": "I'd like you to see physiotherapy as well, and I'll write the referral. The thing that would worry me is if you get numbness between the legs or trouble passing urine. If that happens, go to emergency. Alright, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.84,
      "end_seconds": 360.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}